      "content": "It sounds like you are navigating a profound and deeply disorienting transition after such a long period of intense focus and routine. This feeling of emptiness and detachment is a very natural response when a major, sustained part of your life suddenly changes. Please know that what you are feeling is valid, and allowing yourself to feel this quiet space is a part of the healing process. If you feel overwhelmed by this emptiness, reaching out to a grief counselor or therapist can provide a safe space to begin understanding these new feelings.",
